## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 10.T01

- [ ] **10.T01.** Resolve the CAD reconciliation decisions above. Prove the small native sketch/constraint → extrusion → Boolean workflow through the kernel-neutral adapter, evaluating ezpz and one mesh CSG candidate first as recommended by the Record. Persist source intent, exercise an authorized dimension change and label approximation/unsupported operations; this prototype alone does not complete exact CAD.

### Task 10.T02

- [ ] **10.T02.** Run the recorded OCCT/Rust-kernel bake-off, adding SolidCraft 0.16.0's kernel facade and required vendored `truck` changes as a Rust candidate beside direct `truck`/the retained Rust choices. Choose one buildable, licensed exact-CAD adapter with a maintainable patch boundary and the agreed packaging/execution/failure/cancellation behavior. Keep its dependencies outside the common viewer; source inspection does not preselect the result.

### Task 10.T03

- [ ] **10.T03.** Implement sketch constraints/DOF diagnostics and the initial extrude/revolve/hole/Boolean feature set, native parameter/feature tools, dimension units, failed-feature recovery and incremental recompute. Complete the precise-authoring contract for this supported sketch/curve subset, including normalized residuals, bounded component solves and explicit unresolved geometry. Compare the retained ezpz-first solver, useful CADCraft algorithms and SolidCraft's constructive propagation/rigid-cluster reduction plus bounded residual solve on B10/B23/B29. Preserve branch continuity, distinguish proved elimination from an initial guess, verify all constraints and restore physical free DOF after any numerical gauge removal. Bound construction work, matrix/row/unknown bytes and iterations; do not silently substitute a solver or reuse fixed CAD millimeter tolerances at all scales. Preserve invalid features and expose repair instead of deleting later history.

### Task 10.T04

- [ ] **10.T04.** Add stable semantic feature/face references, validated operation-origin history and explicit ambiguous remapping repair for material regions, mounts and downstream features. Implement complete-boundary/profile selectors with hole/orientation semantics and refusal of partial/duplicate matches; prove the supported B29 subset. Extend B30 surface planning only for selected analytic/trimmed forms, with bounded shared-edge sampling, measured error and CPU fallback. Evaluate GPU execution only on an actual measured gap through the existing Bevy device. Prove the named STEP/render exchange subset and retain original source/feature data with honest loss reports.

### Task 10.T05

- [ ] **10.T05.** Add declared replay/reference outputs, kernel crash/cancel/restart, malicious geometry limits and same-input operation benchmarks for the selected adapters. Include the new manifold-rust candidate only through the bounded mesh comparison; test B24 touching/coplanar/thin-wall/self-difference cases, achieved metric error and topology/correspondence separately. Use B32 to compare analytic/prismatic reductions and general routes against independent references, with units/tolerance/history and whole-operation work recorded. Complete B31 CAD drag previews/final-target acceptance and B24 incremental-versus-from-source checks. Separate exact supported reductions, estimated freeform fitting, unknown correspondence and sampled plausibility. Record actual guarantee levels instead of asserting every kernel is bitwise deterministic. Include required licenses/credits in the CAD Sand. Use H6/B35/B36 with two CAD editors, superseded source/selection, local preview privacy, retained conflicting feature drafts, scoped undo and no automatic stale edit after reconnect; no CAD-specific collaboration server. Extend B40 to supported CAD-derived mesh editing using the same native selected/shared scope, source-variant preparation, provenance and undo, with no false claim that arbitrary sculpting preserves exact constraints.

